title: Ghostscript Spawning a Shell - Upload2Shell Sandbox Escape
id: b74e1f60-2c93-4a58-8d0e-6f15ab3c9207
status: experimental
description: Detects Ghostscript (-dSAFER) interpreters that spawn a command shell, the post-exploitation shape of CVE-2026-125396 (Upload2Shell) when a crafted document is rendered through print queues, mail filters or web upload/preview pipelines. Also matches the research marker strings named in the pwn.ai report.
references:
  - https://pwn.ai/upload2shell
  - https://pwn.ai/upload2shell/research.html
  - https://thehackernews.com/2026/11/researchers-demonstrate-ghostscript.html
  - https://bugs.ghostscript.com/show_bug.cgi?id=709684
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/23
tags:
  - attack.t1190
  - attack.t1203
  - attack.t1059
logsource:
  category: process_creation
  product: linux
detection:
  selection_parent:
    ParentImage|endswith:
      - '/gs'
      - '/gs-10.07'
      - '/gs-10.05'
  selection_shell_child:
    Image|endswith:
      - '/sh'
      - '/bash'
      - '/dash'
      - '/python3'
  selection_research_marker:
    CommandLine|contains:
      - 'GS_CUPS_PIPE_RCE'
      - 'PATH_CONTROL_BYTES_AFTER'
  condition: (selection_parent and selection_shell_child) or selection_research_marker
falsepositives:
  - Document conversion pipelines that deliberately shell out to wrapped Ghostscript helpers
level: high
